# Discrepancy Fixes Log — Read Before Every Fix

## Rule

Before making ANY change related to:
- Today's Activity vs IB discrepancies
- `paper_trades` P&L, status, close_price, or quantity
- `ib_fills` trigger or reconciliation
- `scheduler.ts`, `credit-spread-scanner.ts`, `reconcile-executions.ts`, `trade-closer.ts`
- `TodayActivityTab.tsx` or `paperTradesApi.ts`
- Any DB patch to `paper_trades` records

**You MUST read `docs/cursor/discrepancy-fixes-log.md` first.**

Search the log for the ticker/symptom before touching anything.

If the symptom already appears in the log:
- Read the root cause column
- Read what regressions were previously introduced
- Do NOT repeat the same fix without understanding why it didn't hold

## After Every Fix

Add a row to `docs/cursor/discrepancy-fixes-log.md` **before committing** — the log entry must be part of the same commit as the code change:
- Date, symptom, root cause, files changed, PR number, any side effects

Do NOT merge the PR and then update the log. If the log update is missing from the commit, the PR is incomplete.

## Why

This codebase has introduced regressions while fixing bugs on multiple consecutive days:
- PR #432 fixed RKLB phantom P&L → introduced 7 falsely-closed credit spreads next morning
- PR #431 fixed ADBE display → used wrong partial-close logic, required PR #434 to undo

The log is the only way to break this cycle.
